### CloudWatch Monitoring Alarms

#### EC2 Status Check Alarm

![EC2 Status Check Alarm](screenshots/07-status-check-alarm.png)

**Alarm:** `ReliabilityLab-EC2-StatusCheck-Failed`

Configured a CloudWatch alarm on `StatusCheckFailed_Instance` using a threshold of **≥ 1 for two consecutive 1-minute periods**. The alarm sends notifications to the `reliability-lab-alerts` SNS topic when an EC2 instance status check failure is detected.

**Purpose:** Detect EC2 instance-level health failures and provide an operational alert for investigation and recovery.

#### High CPU Alarm

![High CPU Alarm](screenshots/08-high-cpu-alarm.png)

**Alarm:** `ReliabilityLab-EC2-HighCPU`

Configured a CloudWatch alarm on `CPUUtilization` using a threshold of **>80% for a 5-minute period**. The alarm sends notifications to the `reliability-lab-alerts` SNS topic when sustained high CPU utilization is detected.

**Purpose:** Identify potential workload saturation or abnormal resource consumption before it affects application availability.
